INSERT INTO _bece_gap_preflight_expected_237(question_id,topic_id,subject_id,exam_type_id,question_text,question_type,options,correct_answer,explanation,difficulty,points,marks,time_limit,command_word,assessment_objective) VALUES
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_001','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','Which option is a natural structure rather than a structure made by people?','multiple_choice','["A. The branching trunk of a tree","B. A classroom desk","C. A block footbridge","D. A bicycle frame"]','A','A tree develops its own load-supporting trunk and branches through natural growth, whereas the other structures are designed and assembled by people. Therefore the correct answer is A: The branching trunk of a tree.','easy',1,1,90,'Identify','AO1'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_002','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','Which object is best classified as a frame structure?','multiple_choice','["A. A whole coconut shell","B. A solid clay brick","C. A mound of compacted soil","D. A classroom stool made from joined legs and rails"]','D','A frame structure carries loads through connected members such as legs and rails, rather than through a continuous shell or a solid mass. Therefore the correct answer is D: A classroom stool made from joined legs and rails.','easy',1,1,90,'Identify','AO1'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_003','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','Why can an empty beverage can support a small load before its wall is crushed?','multiple_choice','["A. Its hollow space creates extra material","B. Its thin continuous shell spreads the load around its surface","C. The printed label carries all the force","D. Air inside permanently prevents deformation"]','B','A shell structure uses its shaped continuous surface to distribute forces efficiently, although a dent or excessive load can make the thin wall buckle. Therefore the correct answer is B: Its thin continuous shell spreads the load around its surface.','medium',1,1,90,'Explain','AO2'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_004','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','A learner is making a wooden stool. Which members transfer the seat load toward the floor?','multiple_choice','["A. The decorative paint only","B. The pencil marks on the seat","C. The legs acting as load-supporting members","D. The unused wood offcuts"]','C','The stool legs form the main load path from the seat to the floor, so their strength, alignment and joints determine whether the stool supports a user safely. Therefore the correct answer is C: The legs acting as load-supporting members.','medium',1,1,90,'Explain','AO2'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_005','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','Which change would usually make a tall model tower more stable?','multiple_choice','["A. Widen its base while keeping heavy parts low","B. Narrow its base and raise its mass","C. Remove every lower brace","D. Place it on an uneven loose surface"]','A','A wider support base and lower centre of gravity make it harder for the line of action of the weight to pass outside the base and overturn the tower. Therefore the correct answer is A: Widen its base while keeping heavy parts low.','medium',1,1,90,'Explain','AO2'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_006','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','Why is a diagonal member added across a rectangular wooden frame?','multiple_choice','["A. It makes every joint flexible","B. It removes the need for accurate joints","C. It increases height without supporting load","D. It forms triangles that resist the frame changing shape"]','D','A rectangle can rack into a sloping shape, but diagonal bracing divides it into triangles whose geometry resists distortion under side loads. Therefore the correct answer is D: It forms triangles that resist the frame changing shape.','medium',1,1,90,'Apply','AO2'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_007','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','A cord in a simple model bridge is pulled tight by a load. How is that member acting?','multiple_choice','["A. As a strut carrying compression","B. As a tie carrying tension","C. As a hinge producing rotation","D. As a shell enclosing a space"]','B','A tie resists a pulling force and is therefore in tension; a strut instead resists a pushing force and is mainly in compression. Therefore the correct answer is B: As a tie carrying tension.','hard',1,1,90,'Explain','AO3'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_008','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','In a simple lever used to lift a stone, what is the role of the pivot?','multiple_choice','["A. It supplies electrical current","B. It is the fixed point about which the lever turns","C. It permanently joins the load to the ground","D. It measures the stone’s temperature"]','B','The pivot or fulcrum provides the turning point, allowing an effort applied at one distance to create a turning effect on the load. Therefore the correct answer is B: It is the fixed point about which the lever turns.','medium',1,1,90,'Identify','AO2'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_009','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','Two card strips are joined with paper fasteners so movement of one moves the other. What has been made?','multiple_choice','["A. A solid mass structure","B. A waterproof shell","C. An electrical insulator","D. A linkage that transfers motion between members"]','D','Pivoted members in a linkage transmit and change motion, which learners can observe by moving one strip and tracking the response of the connected strip. Therefore the correct answer is D: A linkage that transfers motion between members.','medium',1,1,90,'Explain','AO2'),
  ('q_bece_bdt_gap_b001_010','topic_bece_bdt_construction','subj_bece_bdt','exam_bece','Before building a model bridge from drinking straws, what should a learner do first?','multiple_choice','["A. Sketch the design and identify dimensions, joints and loads","B. Join materials randomly before choosing a size","C. Decorate every straw before planning","D. Assume any joint will carry the same load"]','A','A labelled sketch turns the design need into dimensions, member positions, joint choices and an intended load path that can be tested after construction. Therefore the correct answer is A: Sketch the design and identify dimensions, joints and loads.','hard',1,1,90,'Sequence','AO3');
